From 1d3e2d0879fa83c7a3cf2147f9c0369be4f077e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:05:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DisplayPowerController: Fade the screen in when it turns on

With config_animateScreenLights the screen fades out through a black
color layer, but the screen on branch dismisses the layer at once, so
there is no fade in. A timed animation of the layer doesn't work on
slow devices either: the display pipeline stalls for 100-300 ms at a
time right after the panel turns on, so most of the animation frames
never reach the display and the fade looks like a jump.

Once the display state is applied, step the layer out in 8 steps. Each
step waits until the previous one is on the display, which the
transaction completed callback and its present fence report, and has
been shown for at least 40 ms, or for at most 600 ms if the callback
doesn't come.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
